# The image's own entries for the security settings the audit log watches (HARDENING in
# /etc/amethystora/security.conf): what Fedora's own services rewrite at every start, recorded and not said. The
# machine's own are in /etc/amethystora/allow.d/hardening (ame security allow hardening PATH). A glob each; these
# are exact paths, so that nothing else in the same folders is quietened.
#
# sssd.service sets the owner and mode of its folders before it starts; ausearch names the two inside
# /etc/sssd from where chmod -R stood, //conf.d and //pki
/etc/sssd
/etc/sssd/conf.d
/etc/sssd/pki
//conf.d
//pki
# tuned writes the module options of its profile when it applies one
/etc/modprobe.d/tuned.conf
